# oracle: fix colvars on examples/PACKAGES/colvars/in.peptide-colvars, shortened (runs of 20 and 10 steps, then the fix redefined with input out.colvars.state output out2 for 10 more): the peptide.colvars distances with a harmonic restraint, a distanceVec whose group2 is $(atoms) and a cartesian component added by fix_modify config, with fix setforce on the reference atom, fix shake and fix nvt; the second run repeats step 20 in the traj (Colvars does not advance at the start of a run), the second state file is kept as out.colvars.state.old, the redefined fix reads the state (its unknown colvars three and four are discarded) and writes out2.* (its thermo_style adds press: the rows of the first two runs are compared through the traj file)
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native: thermo 2.3e-9 (press at step 40; the colvars values at step 0 are identical), final atoms 4.7e-8 (PPPM and SHAKE dynamics of 40 steps from pair sums in another order).
# oracle-examples: PACKAGES/colvars/data.peptide PACKAGES/colvars/peptide.colvars
# oracle-files: out.colvars.traj out.colvars.state out.colvars.state.old out2.colvars.traj out2.colvars.state
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 filerel=1e-9
units           real
atom_style      full
pair_style      lj/charmm/coul/long 8.0 10.0 10.0
bond_style      harmonic
angle_style     charmm
dihedral_style  charmm
improper_style  harmonic
kspace_style    pppm 0.0001
read_data       data.peptide
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    delay 5
timestep        2.0
group           peptide type <= 12
group           one id 2 4 5 6
group           two id 80 82 83 84
group           ref id 37
group           colvar union one two ref
fix             1 all nvt temp  275.0 275.0 100.0 tchain 1
shell           "rm -f out*.colvars.*"
fix             2 all colvars peptide.colvars
fix             2a ref setforce 0.0 0.0 0.0
fix             4 all shake 0.0001 10 100 b 4 6 8 10 12 14 18 a 31
fix_modify      2 config """
  colvar {
    name three
    distanceVec {
      group1 { atomNumbers 80 82 83 84 }
      group2 { atomNumbers $(atoms) }
    }
  }
  colvar {
    name four
    cartesian {
      atoms { atomNumbers 80 82 }
    }
  }
"""
thermo_style    custom step temp etotal pe ke epair ebond &
                f_2 f_2[1][1] f_2[2][1] &
                f_2[3][1] f_2[3][2] f_2[3][3] &
                f_2[4][1] f_2[4][2] f_2[4][3] f_2[4][4] f_2[4][5] f_2[4][6]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             20
run             10
fix 2           all colvars peptide.colvars input out.colvars.state output out2
thermo_style    custom step temp etotal pe ke epair ebond press f_2 f_2[1][1] f_2[2][1]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             10
